# Where the backend is. Copy to .env, or paste the value into Lovable's env settings.
#
# LEAVE IT UNSET for local development: `bun run dev` proxies /worlds to the backend on :8080, so
# every request is same-origin and no CORS is involved. Override the proxy target with BACKEND_URL
# instead — VITE_API_BASE is for deployed origins.
#
# SET IT to point the Lovable preview at the hosted backend. Requests then go absolute and
# cross-origin, so the backend must allow the preview's origin, including POST with
# Content-Type: application/json (which preflights).
#
# Setting it also takes fixture mode off the table: a configured base is a statement that a backend
# exists at that address, so if it cannot be reached the app says so and names the address rather
# than quietly serving bundled captures.
#
# A trailing slash and stray whitespace are tolerated.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=https://your-backend.up.railway.app
